A better target is the 128-channel projection kernel. It currently does five separate small `tl.dot`s per hidden tile. I’m adding a variant that computes projection and gate pairs together (`left+left_gate`, `right+right_gate`) and splits the result inside Triton, reducing dot-call overhead while preserving the same math.
